00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.060
I'm like a visual person, I guess.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.280
I could see the world through visuals.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.540
- But not everybody sees like that.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.980
Not every, like me, we are opposite.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.450
Like, I didn't do any of this.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.985
Candice did.
(Gwen laughing)

00:00:40.985 --> 00:00:42.267
And so, I don't see like that, like-

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.640
- [Gwen] And It's weird for me
that you don't see like that.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.810
Like, I'm like, how?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.920
How do you not see like that?

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.753
- [Kelly] I know but-
- like, just the way I am.

00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:48.630
- [Kelly] But it's art.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.790
It's like some people don't see that.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.950
- I've always been like
a thrift store shopper.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.984
Like, I just love anything vintage.

00:00:54.984 --> 00:00:55.817
- I came out looking different.

00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:57.180
- [Gwen] Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.950
- I shop through thrift stores too, Gwen.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.890
But like, I didn't even
come out looking like this.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.400
I came out looking like,
"She went to a thrift store."

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.750
It was very different.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.550
But I love that it's all organic for you.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.313
I love that you have the
line. That's so cool.

00:01:10.313 --> 00:01:11.370
And you have like your signature look

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.540
that everybody loves too.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.837
I think when I saw you on Instagram

00:01:13.837 --> 00:01:14.670
when you first came out that it

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.540
was like your signature
red-like lip look that came out.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.880
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] That was so cool.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:18.713
- And I-

00:01:18.713 --> 00:01:19.890
- for all of us nerds were like, you know,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.690
we were like, yeah, just a girl.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:22.523
Like, you know, back in the day,

00:01:22.523 --> 00:01:23.427
like, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:25.050
And you think you were weird back then,

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.100
but all of us were weird,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.600
and you made us feel like we weren't,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.002
so that's what was so cool about you.

00:01:29.002 --> 00:01:30.177
- [Gwen] Aw.
- Anyway, that's all.

00:01:30.177 --> 00:01:32.196
(audience cheering)

00:01:32.196 --> 00:01:33.990
But, we thought we'd run through

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.070
some of your past looks, though,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.870
to get the stories behind
them, so is that okay?

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.010
- [Gwen] Yes.
- Okay, okay.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.090
So, let's start with this one.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.320
From your No Doubt days.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.190
So where did this look?

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.397
What were you thinking?

00:01:42.397 --> 00:01:44.128
(audience cheering)

00:01:44.128 --> 00:01:45.420
- [Gwen] It feels like yesterday.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.730
I mean, honestly, time just goes so fast.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.570
- [Kelly] It does.
- [Gwen] It's crazy.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.340
I mean, honestly back then, like I said,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.530
I didn't have a stylist
or a makeup artist.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.780
And once we started
really getting on tour,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.080
like we basically did the
"Just a Girl" video, right?

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.030
And it was our first video really,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.800
and went to the airport,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.900
and then I didn't come home
for like two and a half years.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.160
Like, we were on tour.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.180
Like, it was like, bye.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.507
Like, "Mom, I'll be back."

00:02:07.507 --> 00:02:08.517
"No, I'm not."

00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:11.010
And I still lived at home and I was 26.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.080
So I didn't, because I was gone on tour,

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.060
but all my stuff was there.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.640
And so, when we were on tour, it was like,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.280
well, after a while I needed
clothes, you know what I mean?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.480
Like, I needed costumes.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.190
We'd wear the same thing
over and over again.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.020
Everyone smelled like, it was like-

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:25.853
- Yep.

00:02:25.853 --> 00:02:27.352
- It was like I was super unorganized.

00:02:27.352 --> 00:02:28.185
I have one makeup.
- I have shared

00:02:28.185 --> 00:02:29.550
a bus with boys.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.836
- [Gwen] Yes. It's disgusting.

00:02:30.836 --> 00:02:31.669
- It's Different.

00:02:31.669 --> 00:02:33.690
- [Gwen] But those actual pants,

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.640
I think that was when I found this girl

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.190
through my manager that would
just make clothes for me.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.780
So like, she would go downtown,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.880
she would send me like
literally a piece of paper

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.890
with like swatches stapled to it.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.230
And I'd say, "Okay, do these pants."

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.670
And I would do it from the road.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.072
And then, she would FedEx
out a pair of pants.

00:02:50.072 --> 00:02:50.905
- I love that

00:02:50.905 --> 00:02:52.680
- [Gwen] It was very homegrown.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:53.513
Like, no-

00:02:53.513 --> 00:02:54.390
- [Kelly] I know. But that's
what I mean, it's so natural.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.130
And then you had a
line, it all made sense.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.440
But I love that you look like
you're just so rock and roll.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.970
Like, the person that
passes you on the street,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.920
they're like, "Man, I
wanna look like that."

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.090
And then, you just walk on stage.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.350
Like, that's what I loved about this look.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.846
That was my input right there.

00:03:05.846 --> 00:03:07.860
But wait, what was the occasion here?

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.260
I love this dress so much.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.351
- [Gwen] Okay, that is-

00:03:11.351 --> 00:03:12.270
- [Kelly] This is is so pretty.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.443
- [Gwen] That's Janina.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.233
- Wow.
- [Gwen] Thank you.

00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.160
The designer is Janina.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.979
That was my first public date
with Blake Shelton, actually.

00:03:20.979 --> 00:03:22.217
(audience screaming)

00:03:22.217 --> 00:03:23.180
- I didn't know that.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.887
- [Gwen] It was.
- I love that

00:03:24.887 --> 00:03:27.810
- And it was the Oscar's
Vanity Fair Party.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.280
I think I played at the party,

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.170
and then we went out that night so.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.940
It was like, he never does red carpet,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.900
now that I know him.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.960
Like, that was like, I
think we did a red carpet.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.520
It was kind of a red carpet.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.040
It was raining that night and yeah,

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.030
- [Kelly] You look beautiful.
- I'll always,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.800
like that melts me when I see it,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.955
because it's like such
a moment for me, yeah.

00:03:45.955 --> 00:03:47.813
A good one.
- [Kelly] I didn't know that.

00:03:47.813 --> 00:03:49.560
But you look like Chris
de Burgh, "Lady In Red."

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.610
Like, you're walking in the room,

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.870
and the song was written for you.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.843
Like, that song back in the day.

00:03:52.843 --> 00:03:54.351
I just aged myself, so
- [Gwen] I love that song

00:03:54.351 --> 00:03:56.220
- I love that song so much.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.960
Okay, so wait, where was this shot taken?

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.580
What about this one?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.413
- Okay, that's-
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:04:00.413 --> 00:04:01.631
- [Gwen] Thank you.
- Yeah.

00:04:01.631 --> 00:04:02.464
(audience hooting)

00:04:02.464 --> 00:04:03.870
- [Gwen] That's Vera Wang.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.703
- [Kelly] I love her.

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.060
- [Gwen] It was at the Met ball this year.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.490
And she's just so talented.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.110
Vera's been doing it for so long.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.820
And so, to be able to work with her,

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.250
it was just amazing to
wear a couture dress

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.083
made for me.

00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:17.130
Like, when the sketch came it was like,

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.240
it looked exactly like that.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.580
Like, they drew my face,
the hair, everything.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.680
And it was weird to go from a sketch

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.548
to like real life.

00:04:23.548 --> 00:04:24.381
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:24.381 --> 00:04:26.970
- And that was one of those crazy moments

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.010
where I was gonna have a makeup artist

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.430
do my makeup and her mom had an emergency,

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.270
and she had to leave.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.370
So I luckily had my makeup bag

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.600
and did my own makeup that night.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.880
So it was one of those like crazy moments.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.713
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.
(audience clapping)

00:04:39.713 --> 00:04:41.220
- It was exciting, but.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.950
- I see another difference between

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.180
I see you came out looking like that

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.429
after you did your makeup.

00:04:46.429 --> 00:04:47.490
(Gwen and Kelly laughing)

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.230
Would've been very different from me.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.858
- I wanna do your makeup.

00:04:50.858 --> 00:04:52.800
- Anyone can 'cause I don't.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:53.880
No, I love that though,

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.320
because I think that's the coolest thing

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.330
about fashion is sometimes we forget,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.880
it's such an art form,
and it's so beautiful,

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.710
and you literally look like
a walking piece of art.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.780
- Honestly, I don't even
think people understand

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.373
like, these designers are so talented

00:05:05.373 --> 00:05:07.920
and creative, and I walked into the room,

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.080
and they had those flowers.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.080
They have like hundreds of 'em
that they had made by hand,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.120
like, deciding where
they're gonna put them.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.956
It was literally-

00:05:15.956 --> 00:05:17.536
- Like in the moment, like
while you're worrying about-

00:05:17.536 --> 00:05:18.369
- [Gwen] Yeah.
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:05:18.369 --> 00:05:21.180
- [Gwen] Yeah. It's just
to me, like, beyond a dream

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.980
to be able to work with someone so gifted

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.360
that has had such an impact.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.450
And, you know, Vera's done
so many wedding dresses,

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.033
and a big part of
people's lives, you know,

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.080
with her vision.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.330
So that was an amazing moment

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.850
and never thought that I would get to-

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.800
- And still pull up that crop top, ma'am.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.390
Bam, bam, bam!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.150
I'm like, after three children, whatever.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.860
So how's it going at "The Voice"?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:44.940
Is it fun this season?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.200
- It's-
- [Kelly] It's weird for me.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.000
- It's weird, you'll
be here talking to you,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.959
like, I feel like I'm
cheating on you or something.

00:05:49.959 --> 00:05:50.792
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:05:50.792 --> 00:05:51.625
- No, I'm so excited.

00:05:51.625 --> 00:05:53.987
I was so excited when
they announced Camila.

00:05:53.987 --> 00:05:55.890
'Cause I was like, "Well, wait,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.290
I feel like the same
kinda personality," yeah.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.010
- I was gonna say, she has
the same mentality as you.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:05.340
Like, she doesn't care about
glam or about what she wear.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.720
Like, she's just kinda like a,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.030
she's just talks a lot
and she's competitive,

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.440
and she's you.
- Yeah, yeah yeah.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:12.273
- [Gwen] Like, yeah.

00:06:12.273 --> 00:06:13.890
- Yeah, I was like when
when she came on the show,

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.474
I was like, I'm so excited
for her to go against Blake.

00:06:16.474 --> 00:06:17.307
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:17.307 --> 00:06:19.140
- Yeah, and actually, it was crazy 'cause,

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.380
like, the first few days,
I felt like it took her

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.570
like a couple days to really get there,

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:28.230
and after the first "Shut
up, Blake" then it was on.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.037
- [Kelly] It was on.
- Finally, she goes,

00:06:30.037 --> 00:06:30.870
"Shut up, Blake."

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.030
And then, it was like this whole like-

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:33.863
- They're open.

00:06:33.863 --> 00:06:35.520
- [Gwen] Thing happened. It was, yeah.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.217
- It's a really great
moment for the rest of us.

00:06:37.217 --> 00:06:38.880
- It feels good to say, "Shut up, Blake."

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.770
- [Kelly] Yeah, it really does.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.500
So wait, so do you ever
feel like you're coaching?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.690
I always feel like,
because we're moms as well,

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.460
do you ever feel like
you're kind of the mama?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.457
You feel like very
maternal with your team?

00:06:48.457 --> 00:06:49.980
- [Gwen] For sure.
- I do.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.060
- For me, honestly.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.920
And I know that you're like this,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.040
and I'm not sure Blake
is 'cause Blake isn't.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.620
But when I coach, when
I'm actually in those,

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.020
like, reality days when we
get to really work with them,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.490
that's like my favorite part.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.130
Like besides glam, obviously,
that's my favorite part.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:08.280
But I love being in there
and watching them grow,

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.260
like, right before my
eyes, and it sometimes-

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.747
- Specially young ones like Carter.

00:07:11.747 --> 00:07:12.580
- [Gwen] Yes.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.830
And sometimes it's like,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.277
you think you're gonna say something like,

00:07:15.277 --> 00:07:16.260
"Why don't you try this?"

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.240
And you're doing that because you have

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.560
the knowledge from all the year.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.660
I do, from all those
years and I look back,

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.850
and it's really fun for
me to go "try this,"

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.170
and then they do it.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.480
And you think in your mind
it's not gonna do anything

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.650
and then it does.
- Yeah.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.670
- [Gwen] And not even just me,

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.500
but the whole room is like "Oh, my gosh."

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.320
Like he came to life, like,
right before our eyes.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.153
So it's-

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.007
- Sometimes you have to instill
that confidence, yeah, yeah.

00:07:37.007 --> 00:07:39.150
- [Gwen] It's a really incredible show.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.430
And I love doing it so much.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:42.570
I'm so happy to be back.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:43.410
- [Kelly] Yeah. I know.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.243
I can't wait.

00:07:44.243 --> 00:07:45.900
I can't wait to watch the chemistry.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.520
And you, so we were talking about,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:48.353
you launched your own line.

00:07:48.353 --> 00:07:50.177
It's called, "GXVE Beauty."
So why did you name it that?

00:07:50.177 --> 00:07:52.260
'Cause I assume you like to give beauty,

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.580
like you give that kinda gift.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.413
That's awesome.
- [Gwen] Yeah,

00:07:54.413 --> 00:07:55.890
it's definitely one of those things.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.410
I feel like, with makeup,

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.960
